Description: Keep swaybar drawing after a run-time font change with an explicit height
 With a bar height set, swaymsg bar <id> font ... froze swaybar: the bar
 kept the frame from before the change, and status updates, workspace
 changes and further font changes no longer showed. On a font change
 swaybar reset its height to force a recompute, then asked for the size
 the bar already had, and sway sends no configure for an unchanged size,
 so swaybar waited for one forever.
 .
 The recompute is now forced only for the automatic height. An explicit
 height doesn't depend on the font.
Author: rego-port-bot <339843353+rego-port-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/compare/master...cfsmp3:sway-regolith:swaybar-font-height-freeze
Last-Update: 2026-11-26
---
--- a/swaybar/ipc.c
+++ b/swaybar/ipc.c
@@ -484,7 +484,11 @@ static bool handle_barconfig_update(struct swaybar *bar, const char *payload,
 			destroy_layer_surface(output);
 			wl_list_remove(&output->link);
 			wl_list_insert(&bar->unused_outputs, &output->link);
-		} else if (!pango_font_description_equal(oldcfg->font_description, newcfg->font_description)) {
+		} else if (!newcfg->height && !pango_font_description_equal(
+				oldcfg->font_description, newcfg->font_description)) {
+			// Only an automatic height depends on the font. Forcing an
+			// update of an explicit height would request the unchanged
+			// size, which the compositor doesn't answer with a configure.
 			output->height = 0;  // force update height
 		}
 	}
